rs/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T13:41:31Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T14:00:45Z","body":"Is it better if we use an internal HboxContainer child and we add the controls directly to it? It will allow using size flags and other Node methods and also showing or hiding a title control easily, we also can allow users to get the hbox container similar to how split container allows getting the dragger control and warns that it cannot be removed. Because It's missing a way to get the title controls count and looping over them or changing their order.\r\n\r\nEdit: Also they will be visible in remote scene tree and it may be useful for debugging.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648023838/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648835748","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102346#issuecomment-2648835748","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102346","id":2648835748,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d4gak","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T18:03:21Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T18:03:21Z","body":"I considered that, but it's an extra internal Control that can be avoided.\r\nAlso what about other title elements? The icon and text would need to be TextureRect and Label. It becomes tricky to manage.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648835748/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648937964","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102346#issuecomment-2648937964","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102346","id":2648937964,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d45Xs","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T18:48:19Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T19:05:45Z","body":"> I considered that, but it's an extra internal Control that can be avoided. Also what about other title elements? The icon and text would need to be TextureRect and Label. It becomes tricky to manage.\r\n\r\nThe reason why i avoided using other Control nodes for icon and title is that they will consume a lot of ram if we have many instances of it, the plan was to replace the editor inspector sections, and to optimize the project and editor settings with it, I believe you can end up with the best solution that doesn't come with a cost when it's used all over the editor, we can first implement it as an editor only class similar to the EditorSpinSlider, this will give us more freedom to shape the class without breaking compatibility and after that, we can register it.\r\n\r\nEdit: by saying optimize Editor and Project settings with it i just mean we organize them in a better way.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648937964/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648984791","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102346#issuecomment-2648984791","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102346","id":2648984791,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d5EzX","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T19:09:02Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T19:13:52Z","body":"> * The title height changes if there's no text, which looks a bit strange when you're typing titles in the editor. To avoid this, you could set the minimum height to the font ascent of the title font by querying it with TextServer. Notice how the last FoldableContainer is smaller compared to the others:\r\n\r\n\r\nI tried to follow the same way the button works, so if no text, it will fallback to the minimum left icon size, and you can make it much smaller if you override the icon to a smaller one, we can have a property `minimum_title_height` to solve this.\r\n\r\nEdit: I think a theme constant will be better than a property.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648984791/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2649974531","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102346#issuecomment-2649974531","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102346","id":2649974531,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d82cD","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T07:02:17Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T07:02:17Z","body":"> It's not very accessible on a controller, but it's OK on a keyboard (since you can use Tab and Shift + Tab.\r\n\r\nWhat if we add `L1` and `R1` to `ui_focus_(prev/next)` actions?\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2649974531/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"